    "research": {
      "notes": "Searches found little dated inside 2026-09-15 to 2026-10-15 for topics 1, 3, 4 and 6. Most of what surfaced is older context, and I flag it as such.\n\n## 1. Guidance\n- Nothing new in the window. No pre-announcement, cut or withdrawal found. \nThe next earnings report is listed for 2026-11-25.\n (2026-10-15, https://www.investing.com/equities/nvidia-corp-earnings)\n- Prior to the window, Q2 FY27 revenue was \n$96.2B\n — 2026-08-26 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001045810/000104581026000073/q2fy27pr.htm\n- Q3 guidance was \n$108B ±2% versus $104.2B expected\n. The outlook \nincludes no China data center sales\n. — 2026-08-26 — https://www.cnbc.com/2026/08/26/nvidia-nvda-earnings-report-q2-2027-live-updates.html\n- \nThe CFO guided FY28 revenue growth of about 70% versus 44% expected.\n — 2026-08-26 — same CNBC URL\n\n## 2. Analyst actions\n- Exane BNP Paribas (Karl Ackerman) raised its target to $345 from $285 and kept a Buy. — 2026-10-05 — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/nvda/forecast\n- Yorkville Ives & Co (Daniel Ives) initiated at Buy with a $300 target. — 2026-10-06 — same TipRanks URL\n- Citi (Atif Malik) reiterated Buy, $315. — 2026-10-06 — same URL\n- UBS (Timothy Arcuri) reiterated Buy, $300. — 2026-10-09 — same URL\n- Morgan Stanley (Joseph Moore) \nraised its target\n and holds Overweight. The new figure and date are not given. — date unknown (article ~2026-10-13) — https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nvidia-just-hit-buy-point-143021491.html\n- Consensus target figures differ by source:\n  - \n$329.34 mean, 69 analysts\n — 2026-09-23 — https://www.chartmill.com/stock/quote/NVDA/analyst-ratings\n  - \n$324.20 average, 33 analysts, high $465, low $275\n — about 2026-10-09 — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/nvda/forecast\n  - \n$327.70, Yahoo Finance average of 61 analysts\n — about 2026-09-30 — https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nvidia-price-targets-higher-analysts-123002439.html\n\n## 3. Litigation and regulation\n- No new lawsuits, fines or investigations dated in the window.\n- Export-control background (earlier than the window):\n  - \nUS licences allow up to 75,000 H200 chips per approved China buyer.\n — 2026-05-14 — https://www.cnbc.com/2026/05/14/us-clears-h200-chip-sales-to-10-china-firms-as-nvidia-ceo-looks-for-breakthrough.html\n  - \nA \"trivial\" number of H200s had shipped, per Commerce Under Secretary Kessler.\n — 2026-07-14 — https://finance.yahoo.com/technology/ai/articles/small-amount-nvidia-ai-chips-152915216.html\n- China's antitrust finding on the Mellanox deal dates to 2025-09-15; I found no resolution in the window. — https://techcrunch.com/2025/09/15/china-says-nvidia-violated-antitrust-regulations\n\n## 4. Customer concentration\n- No new customer win, loss or contract change dated in the window.\n- One secondary source says three direct customers were \n21%, 17% and 16% of Q1 FY27 revenue\n. I did not check this against the 10-Q. — date unknown (Q1 FY27 ended 2026-04-26) — https://www.mexc.com/learn/article/nvidia-customer-concentration-explained-hyperscalers-ai-clouds-and-the-risk-behind-data-center-growth/1\n- Q2 Data Center revenue was \n$89B, with hyperscale revenue more than doubling\n. — 2026-08-26 — https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nvidia-nvda-prove-doesn-t-202105317.html\n- Reported Nvidia–OpenAI deal talks (Feb 2026) are outside the window. — https://www.cnbc.com/2026/02/03/nvidia-openai-stalled-on-their-mega-deal-ai-giants-need-each-other.html\n\n## 5. Insider activity (all sales; no purchases found)\n- Director Mark Stevens sold about 1.37M shares, \n1,356,000 at $219.72 and 10,000 at $220.42\n. They were sold from a trust. — 2026-09-18 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001045810/000119903926000016/wk-form4_1790110579.xml\n- Timothy Teter's Form 4 reports sales \nunder a 10b5-1 plan adopted 2026-05-22\n, at roughly $221.59–$224.00 a share. His earlier Form 4 was signed 2026-09-02, and that signing date is the only date shown. Sale dates are not stated. — filed 2026-09-23 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001045810/000169684126000014/wk-form4_1790196985.xml\n- An unnamed reporting person sold under a \n10b5-1 plan adopted 2026-06-16\n at roughly $217–$220 a share. The sale date and the reporting person's name are not shown in the excerpt. — date unknown — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001045810/000158867026000014/wk-form4_1789765959.xml\n- EVP Nicholas Parker received an RSU grant on 2026-09-09. It was \n172,507 shares\n in the original filing. A \nForm 4/A corrects an administrative error in the share count\n, giving \n160,418\n. — 2026-09-09 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001045810/000215218826000005/wk-form4_1789160684.xml and https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001045810/000215218826000007/wk-form4a_1791925767.xml\n- I found no Jensen Huang Form 4 dated in the window.\n\n## 6. Product and competitive\n- Nvidia published an open rack design (MGX) the same week as an AMD-backed shared data-hall plan. \nTwo open rack designs now exist: Nvidia's MGX and the Meta-backed design AMD uses.\n — about 2026-10-14 — https://forbes.com/sites/jonmarkman/2026/10/14/nvidia-opens-its-vera-rubin-rack-design-to-speed-up-ai-data-centers\n- \nVera Rubin is \"in full production.\"\n — 2026-08-26 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001045810/000104581026000073/q2fy27pr.htm\n- Rubin delay rumours and AMD Helios/MI455X competition come from older or lower-quality sources (wccftech, Aug 2025 AInvest, Network World), so I haven't relied on them.",
